WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.020
If the organizer sends a signal, the signal should be a substance.

2
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:09.020
So kill the cells.

3
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:10.840
Does it still work?

4
00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:18.010
From 1933, Johannes Holtfreter froze, dried and heated pieces of newt embryos, some

5
00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:19.010
to boiling.

6
00:00:19.533 --> 00:00:22.273
He placed them against early-gastrula ectoderm.

7
00:00:23.113 --> 00:00:25.253
On its own, that ectoderm became skin.

8
00:00:26.317 --> 00:00:29.777
Next to dead organizer, does the ectoderm become neural?

9
00:00:30.577 --> 00:00:32.077
And does a second axis form?

10
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:40.530
The ectoderm often became neural.

11
00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:44.610
A living organizer was not needed for the neural response.

12
00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:48.530
But in these tests, organizing did not survive.

13
00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:53.850
Killed tissue made ectoderm neural without building an organized second axis.

14
00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:02.480
A factor is sufficient if it is enough, by itself, to produce an effect.

15
00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.460
It is necessary if that effect does not happen without it.

16
00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:10.590
Dead organizer was sufficient to make ectoderm neural.

17
00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:13.110
But sufficient does not mean natural.

18
00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:15.230
Then the controls were run.

19
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.400
Many other killed tissues induced too.

20
00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:23.060
So did ether extracts of amphibian tissue, in the 1930s.

21
00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:29.090
Unrelated materials, from adult tissues to synthetic chemicals, induced in some

22
00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:30.090
cases.

23
00:01:30.583 --> 00:01:36.623
In the 1940s, salamander ectoderm became neural with no organizer at all, or after

24
00:01:36.623 --> 00:01:37.623
brief damage.

25
00:01:38.317 --> 00:01:41.997
When almost everything scores yes, a yes cannot name the signal.

26
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.160
Waddington described the trap.

27
00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:54.380
Perhaps competent ectoderm already holds a hidden tendency to become neural.

28
00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:57.890
Then a substance might be the natural signal.

29
00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:01.770
Or it might merely injure the tissue, and release that tendency.

30
00:02:02.883 --> 00:02:07.663
The salamander result is one explanation for why the chemical hunt stalled for

31
00:02:07.663 --> 00:02:08.663
decades.

32
00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:12.933
Suppose neural is what ectoderm becomes when a brake is released.

33
00:02:13.853 --> 00:02:18.293
Then many injuries and chemicals that weaken it would be expected to induce too.

34
00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:27.987
The next lesson shows frog ectoderm, its cells separated, becoming neural with no

35
00:02:27.987 --> 00:02:28.987
inducer at all.

36
00:02:29.817 --> 00:02:33.097
So neighbours can set a cell's fate, while it can still answer.

37
00:02:33.997 --> 00:02:35.317
What the signal is comes next.
